1
00:00:05,100 --> 00:00:12,100
[THEME MUSIC PLAYING]

2
00:00:31,833 --> 00:00:32,800
[TIRES SCREECHING]

3
00:00:34,267 --> 00:00:35,233
[ENGINE REVVING]

4
00:00:39,933 --> 00:00:40,833
[TIRES SCREECH]

5
00:00:42,633 --> 00:00:43,933
[ENGINES REVVING]

6
00:00:43,933 --> 00:00:45,333
[TRUCK HORN BLARES]

7
00:00:45,333 --> 00:00:46,300
[LOUD CRASH]

8
00:00:46,933 --> 00:00:48,467
[TIRES SCREECHING]

9
00:00:50,867 --> 00:00:51,833
[GUNSHOT]

10
00:00:52,867 --> 00:00:54,000
[FIREWORKS EXPLODING]

11
00:00:54,000 --> 00:00:55,633
- [ENGINES REVVING]
- [BUS HORN HONKS]

12
00:00:56,833 --> 00:00:57,900
[GLASS SHATTERING]

13
00:00:58,500 --> 00:01:00,467
- [TIRES SCREECHING]
- [LOUD CRASH]

14
00:01:01,300 --> 00:01:02,833
[ENGINES REVVING]

15
00:01:05,200 --> 00:01:06,233
[TIRES SCREECHING]

16
00:01:08,533 --> 00:01:09,533
[TIRES SCREECHING]

17
00:01:10,333 --> 00:01:11,467
- [GUNSHOT]
- [TIRES SCREECHING]

18
00:01:11,900 --> 00:01:13,333
- [TRUCK HORN BLARES]
- [LOUD CRASH]

19
00:01:13,333 --> 00:01:14,533
[TIRES SCREECHING]

20
00:01:20,033 --> 00:01:21,533
<i> I am the man of the house.</i>

21
00:01:21,533 --> 00:01:23,400
<i> I should be the one working.</i>

22
00:01:23,400 --> 00:01:24,800
<i>It's embarrassing
to admit but...</i>

23
00:01:24,800 --> 00:01:27,300
your Auntie Betchay is the one
making money to provide for us.

24
00:01:27,300 --> 00:01:29,033
<i> Don't lose hope.</i>

25
00:01:29,033 --> 00:01:30,700
<i> I'm here to help you.</i>

26
00:01:30,700 --> 00:01:32,667
<i> One day, I hope you find...</i>

27
00:01:32,667 --> 00:01:35,533
a woman who will truly love you
<i> and change your life.</i>

28
00:01:35,533 --> 00:01:37,833
<i>They're already building up
a case against you.</i>

29
00:01:37,833 --> 00:01:39,133
<i> To kick you out of the agency.</i>

30
00:01:39,133 --> 00:01:42,033
<i>Maybe we could try to use it
as evidence against Mr. Chan</i>

31
00:01:42,067 --> 00:01:43,700
<i> if we find that gold.</i>

32
00:01:44,367 --> 00:01:45,500
<i> I'm a bit tipsy.</i>

33
00:01:45,500 --> 00:01:46,733
<i> I'll bring Sam home.</i>

34
00:01:46,733 --> 00:01:49,733
<i>Sir, we don't have grounds
to stop them</i>

35
00:01:49,733 --> 00:01:51,333
<i> from talking to Victor Zafra.</i>

36
00:01:51,333 --> 00:01:53,400
<i> A group of men ambushed me</i>

37
00:01:53,400 --> 00:01:57,900
<i>because I called out
Ricardo Jacinto and the police</i>

38
00:01:57,900 --> 00:02:00,333
<i> regarding the demolishment
at Ginintuang Lupa.</i>

39
00:02:00,333 --> 00:02:02,033
<i>The project seems to be less
and less possible.</i>

40
00:02:02,033 --> 00:02:03,367
<i>You're successful
in your career,</i>

41
00:02:03,367 --> 00:02:04,700
<i> but not in business.</i>

42
00:02:05,933 --> 00:02:08,033
[BOSS 1] Make sure you've got
all your stuff ready

43
00:02:08,033 --> 00:02:09,500
so we don't run into delays.

44
00:02:09,500 --> 00:02:10,433
[MEN SHOUTING]

45
00:02:10,433 --> 00:02:12,000
Get everything prepared now.

46
00:02:12,000 --> 00:02:14,033
They're coming,
and I want all of you set.

47
00:02:14,067 --> 00:02:16,367
[BOSS 2] Hey, why are there
so few of them?

48
00:02:16,367 --> 00:02:18,767
Grab more
so we can hit the quota.

49
00:02:18,767 --> 00:02:20,767
[GOON 1] Boss, we're drawing too
much attention from the cops,

50
00:02:20,767 --> 00:02:22,733
especially around Makati
and BGC.

51
00:02:22,733 --> 00:02:24,067
Then go to Tondo.

52
00:02:24,067 --> 00:02:25,767
Nobody will notice them.

53
00:02:25,767 --> 00:02:27,400
What matters is
we reach the quota.

54
00:02:27,400 --> 00:02:28,300
- [GOON 1] Copy, boss.
- Good.

55
00:02:28,300 --> 00:02:31,367
Now, check them
so we can get started.

56
00:02:31,367 --> 00:02:32,633
[INDISTINCT SHOUTING]

57
00:02:32,633 --> 00:02:39,600
[DARK MUSIC PLAYING]

58
00:02:40,067 --> 00:02:41,933
- [GOON 2] Come on, quickly!
- [GOON 3] Next, next!

59
00:02:41,933 --> 00:02:44,367
[BOSS 2] This one looks good.

60
00:02:44,367 --> 00:02:46,100
- [GOON 4] Copy that.
- Get it done immediately!

61
00:02:46,100 --> 00:02:49,100
Begin the operation
so we can profit from them.

62
00:02:49,133 --> 00:02:50,067
[GOON 5] Follow me!

63
00:02:55,733 --> 00:02:57,600
Thank you, my dear.

64
00:02:57,600 --> 00:02:59,400
[GLOOMY MUSIC PLAYING]

65
00:02:59,400 --> 00:03:02,400
I knew you
couldn't turn me down.

66
00:03:03,100 --> 00:03:05,067
Just like old times.

67
00:03:06,833 --> 00:03:08,033
[MARIANO] Who was that?

68
00:03:08,767 --> 00:03:09,767
[DEBORAH SIGHS HEAVILY]

69
00:03:09,767 --> 00:03:12,100
[MUSIC BECOMES SUSPENSEFUL]

70
00:03:12,100 --> 00:03:16,567
The trump card I told you about,
and it turns out...

71
00:03:16,967 --> 00:03:18,467
it's a winning card.

72
00:03:18,467 --> 00:03:20,100
Be straight with me, Deborah.

73
00:03:20,100 --> 00:03:21,633
Who was that?

74
00:03:23,000 --> 00:03:24,800
An insider...

75
00:03:25,700 --> 00:03:27,800
...from NCIA.

76
00:03:27,800 --> 00:03:28,700
[MARIANO] Hmm?

77
00:03:28,700 --> 00:03:31,700
Now, stop pressing me
with questions.

78
00:03:31,700 --> 00:03:37,100
What matters is
the intel I picked up.

79
00:03:37,100 --> 00:03:39,100
- Hmm. That'll do.
- [GLASSES CLINK]

80
00:03:39,767 --> 00:03:40,767
[SNICKERS]

81
00:03:43,633 --> 00:03:45,433
[MUSIC FADES]

82
00:03:51,433 --> 00:03:52,367
[CAR DOOR CLOSES]

83
00:03:52,367 --> 00:03:54,000
I'll escort you in.

84
00:03:54,000 --> 00:03:56,633
Your parents might say
I'm not looking after you.

85
00:03:56,667 --> 00:03:58,067
- [SAM SCOFFS] Seriously?
- [TWINKLE] Oh...

86
00:03:58,067 --> 00:03:59,633
- Ma'am Sam.
- [TOTO CHUCKLES SOFTLY]

87
00:03:59,633 --> 00:04:04,167
[TOTO]
Who's this fine-looking guy?

88
00:04:04,167 --> 00:04:05,167
I'm Sebastian.

89
00:04:05,167 --> 00:04:07,200
Oh, you're so handsome, sir!

90
00:04:07,200 --> 00:04:09,000
Such a beautiful smile!

91
00:04:09,000 --> 00:04:10,033
Of course.

92
00:04:10,033 --> 00:04:11,833
Sam deserves nothing less
than a handsome man.

93
00:04:11,833 --> 00:04:12,733
[GIGGLES SOFTLY]

94
00:04:12,733 --> 00:04:14,733
- Let's go. Excuse me.
- Sure thing...

95
00:04:14,733 --> 00:04:15,800
[TWINKLE] Yes.

96
00:04:15,800 --> 00:04:17,533
- [LIGHT MUSIC PLAYING]
- [BREATHES DEEPLY]

97
00:04:17,533 --> 00:04:19,733
- [TOTO] Sweetie! Sweetie!
- [GIGGLING]

98
00:04:19,733 --> 00:04:23,000
Ma'am Sam is getting
into the dating scene!

99
00:04:23,000 --> 00:04:23,900
[TOTO CHUCKLES]

100
00:04:23,900 --> 00:04:26,200
[CATALAN] Don't you have
another daughter?

101
00:04:26,200 --> 00:04:27,633
Your youngest?

102
00:04:27,667 --> 00:04:30,000
[RICARDO] Oh, you mean Samantha.

103
00:04:30,567 --> 00:04:31,733
Yes, that's her.

104
00:04:31,733 --> 00:04:33,100
I saw her on the news.

105
00:04:33,100 --> 00:04:36,167
She's impressive,
bringing down a big fish.

106
00:04:36,167 --> 00:04:38,067
- [MOROSE MUSIC PLAYING]
- [INDISTINCT CROWD CHATTER]

107
00:04:38,067 --> 00:04:39,833
[CATALAN] I'm sure
you're proud of her work.

108
00:04:39,833 --> 00:04:41,100
- Can you manage?
- I'm okay.

109
00:04:41,100 --> 00:04:42,733
- Just walk straight.
- [RICARDO] Of course.

110
00:04:42,733 --> 00:04:44,000
The Jacinto blood runs
through her.

111
00:04:44,000 --> 00:04:45,033
[EXHALES SOFTLY]

112
00:04:47,033 --> 00:04:48,500
[ISOBEL] Oh, Sam!

113
00:04:50,100 --> 00:04:53,067
Oh, Sam, we were just
talking about you.

114
00:04:53,733 --> 00:04:54,733
Good evening.

115
00:04:54,733 --> 00:04:55,900
Good evening, everybody.

116
00:04:56,567 --> 00:04:57,867
Agent Jacinto.

117
00:04:58,233 --> 00:05:00,000
Your parents are
very proud of you.

118
00:05:00,767 --> 00:05:03,433
It's a shame you ended up
working for a different agency.

119
00:05:03,867 --> 00:05:04,867
[ISOBEL CHUCKLES]

120
00:05:04,867 --> 00:05:07,000
So, do you think...

121
00:05:07,467 --> 00:05:11,233
she'll make a strong addition
to NLEA if the chance comes?

122
00:05:11,767 --> 00:05:13,000
[CATALAN] Absolutely.

123
00:05:13,233 --> 00:05:14,733
As the General put it,

124
00:05:15,133 --> 00:05:16,933
the Jacinto blood runs
through her.

125
00:05:16,933 --> 00:05:18,100
[MOROSE MUSIC CONTINUES]

126
00:05:18,100 --> 00:05:19,067
[SAM SNICKERS]

127
00:05:19,067 --> 00:05:20,100
You see?

128
00:05:20,100 --> 00:05:22,067
[SAM, ISOBEL CHUCKLING]

129
00:05:22,067 --> 00:05:23,900
Your father is proud of you.

130
00:05:24,867 --> 00:05:25,967
Dear, what happened?

131
00:05:25,967 --> 00:05:27,867
Why are you drunk?

132
00:05:27,867 --> 00:05:28,833
[SIGHS]

133
00:05:30,733 --> 00:05:32,900
[ISOBEL CHUCKLING]

134
00:05:32,900 --> 00:05:35,933
[DEBORAH] According to
my insider from NCIA,

135
00:05:35,967 --> 00:05:39,067
Mr. Chan has consented
to serve as a witness.

136
00:05:39,800 --> 00:05:40,800
What?

137
00:05:40,800 --> 00:05:41,900
[GLASS THUDS]

138
00:05:41,900 --> 00:05:43,733
Does that mean he'll testify
against my brother?

139
00:05:43,733 --> 00:05:44,900
Yes.

140
00:05:45,500 --> 00:05:49,133
He's going to serve
as NCIA's state witness.

141
00:05:49,133 --> 00:05:51,800
It's time to eliminate Mr. Chan.

142
00:05:51,800 --> 00:05:53,600
Violence is the only way now.

143
00:05:53,600 --> 00:05:54,633
I know.

144
00:05:54,633 --> 00:05:58,733
By tomorrow, he'll be moved
to a secured area,

145
00:05:58,733 --> 00:06:02,267
and he'll be under
the witness protection program.

146
00:06:02,267 --> 00:06:04,567
This is your chance, Lucas.

147
00:06:04,567 --> 00:06:06,000
[TENSE MUSIC PLAYING]

148
00:06:06,000 --> 00:06:07,967
Get rid of Mr. Chan.

149
00:06:09,700 --> 00:06:10,833
Arturo.

150
00:06:10,833 --> 00:06:11,933
The rest of you.

151
00:06:11,933 --> 00:06:13,533
Go with Lucas.

152
00:06:13,533 --> 00:06:15,300
I don't want past mistakes
to be repeated.

153
00:06:15,300 --> 00:06:17,167
- [ALL] Yes, sir.
- [DEBORAH] No.

154
00:06:17,167 --> 00:06:18,867
Not Lucas.

155
00:06:18,867 --> 00:06:20,667
You, Mariano!

156
00:06:20,667 --> 00:06:22,667
You should finish the job!

157
00:06:22,667 --> 00:06:26,933
[TENSE MUSIC CONTINUES]

158
00:06:26,933 --> 00:06:27,967
Ma.

159
00:06:28,600 --> 00:06:29,833
You too?

160
00:06:29,833 --> 00:06:31,767
You don't believe in me?

161
00:06:31,767 --> 00:06:33,167
Ma, I can do the job!

162
00:06:34,633 --> 00:06:36,200
Your mother is right.

163
00:06:36,200 --> 00:06:38,067
I will get rid of Mr. Chan.

164
00:06:39,167 --> 00:06:41,133
I have another job for you.

165
00:06:41,900 --> 00:06:43,300
What is it, Papa?

166
00:06:43,300 --> 00:06:45,000
Now is the time

167
00:06:45,000 --> 00:06:48,033
for you to get rid
of Samantha Jacinto.

168
00:06:48,033 --> 00:06:49,033
Wait!

169
00:06:49,033 --> 00:06:52,367
Why do you have
to kill Samantha Jacinto?!

170
00:06:52,367 --> 00:06:56,033
We need to focus on Mr. Chan!

171
00:06:56,033 --> 00:06:58,000
Even though Mr. Chan is gone

172
00:06:58,000 --> 00:07:00,000
and there are
no more witnesses,

173
00:07:00,000 --> 00:07:02,900
Samantha is still
handling the case.

174
00:07:02,900 --> 00:07:05,700
And she'd still target Victor.

175
00:07:05,700 --> 00:07:06,933
You're right, Papa.

176
00:07:07,967 --> 00:07:09,567
Ma,

177
00:07:09,567 --> 00:07:12,167
it would be best to kill both

178
00:07:12,167 --> 00:07:15,133
Mr. Chan and Samantha Jacinto
at the same time.

179
00:07:15,167 --> 00:07:22,733
[TENSE MUSIC CONTINUES]

180
00:07:25,867 --> 00:07:27,900
- [WHISPERS] Go on.
- [MAX] Sam.

181
00:07:27,900 --> 00:07:29,900
- Hmm?
- Who's this?

182
00:07:29,900 --> 00:07:31,733
I didn't know
you brought someone.

183
00:07:31,733 --> 00:07:35,200
- Uh, it's...
- Sorry for crashing your party.

184
00:07:35,200 --> 00:07:37,867
By the way,
let me introduce myself.

185
00:07:37,867 --> 00:07:39,900
I'm top agent Sebastian.

186
00:07:39,900 --> 00:07:42,733
Ah, so you're Sebastian.

187
00:07:42,733 --> 00:07:43,900
- Ah, nice to meet you.
- Oh!

188
00:07:43,900 --> 00:07:45,700
I'm the mom of Sam.

189
00:07:45,700 --> 00:07:48,033
Oh, hello.
Nice to meet you.

190
00:07:48,067 --> 00:07:50,067
You are very beautiful like Sam.

191
00:07:50,067 --> 00:07:51,267
[ISOBEL GIGGLES]

192
00:07:51,267 --> 00:07:53,200
Thank you!

193
00:07:53,200 --> 00:07:56,233
Sir, I'm top agent Sebastian.

194
00:07:56,233 --> 00:07:58,800
You're so good-looking
in person.

195
00:07:58,800 --> 00:07:59,867
What happened to you?

196
00:07:59,867 --> 00:08:01,100
Sebastian?

197
00:08:01,100 --> 00:08:02,867
[PENSIVE MUSIC PLAYING]

198
00:08:02,867 --> 00:08:06,233
Are you the Sebastian
who's courting Sam?

199
00:08:06,233 --> 00:08:07,867
Oh, you're handsome.

200
00:08:07,867 --> 00:08:10,100
Sam, you should be together.

201
00:08:10,100 --> 00:08:11,100
[SAM CHUCKLES AWKWARDLY]

202
00:08:11,100 --> 00:08:12,700
We're just co-workers.

203
00:08:12,700 --> 00:08:13,967
- For now.
- Yes.

204
00:08:13,967 --> 00:08:17,767
I think soon-to-be-boyfriend
sounds better.

205
00:08:17,767 --> 00:08:18,600
Yes.

206
00:08:18,600 --> 00:08:20,967
Because you know,
I'm almost there!

207
00:08:21,000 --> 00:08:22,433
Ooh! Almost there.

208
00:08:23,400 --> 00:08:25,933
[SEBASTIAN]
Uh, again, sorry to interrupt.

209
00:08:25,933 --> 00:08:27,133
I'll get going.

210
00:08:27,133 --> 00:08:29,000
I just brought Sam home

211
00:08:29,000 --> 00:08:30,900
just to make sure
she's home safe.

212
00:08:30,900 --> 00:08:32,233
- Okay.
- I'll get going.

213
00:08:32,233 --> 00:08:34,967
- Go. Bye.
- Oh, no, Sebastian.

214
00:08:34,967 --> 00:08:37,267
You know what,
you seem fun at parties.

215
00:08:37,267 --> 00:08:39,167
- Really?
- Join us, please.

216
00:08:39,167 --> 00:08:41,067
- Sure.
- Would you like-- Ah!

217
00:08:41,067 --> 00:08:45,067
Have this.
This is a very good whiskey...

218
00:08:45,067 --> 00:08:46,300
[SEBASTIAN] Thank you so much.

219
00:08:47,333 --> 00:08:48,667
[OVERLAPPING CHATTER]

220
00:08:48,667 --> 00:08:51,300
Hey, hurry up! Fix the tables!
The kids are hungry!

221
00:08:51,300 --> 00:08:53,400
- You keep nagging!
- You were rushing us.

222
00:08:53,400 --> 00:08:54,933
Go on, dig in.

223
00:08:54,967 --> 00:08:56,333
Here.

224
00:08:56,333 --> 00:08:58,833
- Gabo is so kind.
- [MELLOW MUSIC PLAYING]

225
00:08:58,833 --> 00:08:59,667
That's true.

226
00:08:59,667 --> 00:09:02,800
And you know what,
he helped us too!

227
00:09:02,800 --> 00:09:05,167
He helped us get away
from the cranky vendor!

228
00:09:05,167 --> 00:09:06,167
That cranky lady.

229
00:09:06,167 --> 00:09:09,033
He's my idol! He's strong!

230
00:09:09,033 --> 00:09:10,867
That's true!

231
00:09:10,867 --> 00:09:13,367
When I grow up,
I want to be just like Gabo!

232
00:09:13,367 --> 00:09:16,033
- Oh!
- Me too! Me too! Me too!

233
00:09:16,033 --> 00:09:18,767
[OVERLAPPING CHATTER]

234
00:09:18,767 --> 00:09:20,800
[CAR APPROACHING]

235
00:09:20,800 --> 00:09:21,867
[CAR DOOR OPENS]

236
00:09:21,867 --> 00:09:28,433
- [HEAVY FOOTSTEPS]
- [FOREBODING MUSIC PLAYING]

237
00:09:37,533 --> 00:09:39,700
You're right, kids.

238
00:09:40,733 --> 00:09:42,333
Because when it comes to Gabo...

239
00:09:42,333 --> 00:09:45,367
- Listen to your dad.
- ...trust that I know him well.

240
00:09:45,367 --> 00:09:47,367
I have known him
since he was young.

241
00:09:47,367 --> 00:09:51,033
He's very kind,
and he's a great fighter.

242
00:09:51,033 --> 00:09:53,300
- But most of all...
- What?

243
00:09:53,300 --> 00:09:55,000
I'm as handsome as him.

244
00:09:55,000 --> 00:10:00,333
- [KIDS HOLLERING]
- [LAUGHTER]

245
00:10:01,400 --> 00:10:02,433
[KID] Thief!

246
00:10:02,433 --> 00:10:03,667
Hey! Hey!

247
00:10:03,667 --> 00:10:05,267
- [PEOPLE CLAMORING]
- [MUSIC TURNS TENSE]

248
00:10:05,267 --> 00:10:08,067
- What do you need?!
- Please don't hurt us!

249
00:10:08,067 --> 00:10:09,200
Sir, please!

250
00:10:11,433 --> 00:10:12,533
[BODY THUDS]

251
00:10:14,000 --> 00:10:14,967
[BLOW LANDS]

252
00:10:15,533 --> 00:10:16,467
[BLOW LANDS]

253
00:10:18,367 --> 00:10:21,033
[KIDS WAILING]

254
00:10:23,900 --> 00:10:29,400
[WAILING CONTINUES]

255
00:10:31,033 --> 00:10:32,067
Get the kids away!

256
00:10:40,600 --> 00:10:42,067
Pa!

257
00:10:42,067 --> 00:10:47,600
[TENSE MUSIC CONTINUES]

258
00:10:47,600 --> 00:10:50,267
- [CAR DOOR CLOSES]
- [CAR ENGINE REVS]

259
00:10:50,267 --> 00:10:52,467
- [SOMBER MUSIC PLAYING]
- [VENDOR] Steamed duck eggs!

260
00:10:52,467 --> 00:10:54,067
That was odd.

261
00:10:54,067 --> 00:10:56,800
What was she thinking,
working at BeerGin?

262
00:10:56,800 --> 00:10:59,067
That's why Uncle Rudy got mad.

263
00:10:59,067 --> 00:11:01,933
Gabo, if you take another
mission and get paid,

264
00:11:01,933 --> 00:11:04,367
why don't you just build
Aunt Betchay her own beerhouse?

265
00:11:04,367 --> 00:11:07,133
And build it
right across BeerGin.

266
00:11:07,133 --> 00:11:08,867
Let's just eat at BeerGin.

267
00:11:08,900 --> 00:11:11,500
See? You guys are so bright!

268
00:11:11,500 --> 00:11:13,133
You just gave Aunt Betchay

269
00:11:13,133 --> 00:11:14,833
more reasons to be mad at Gabo!

270
00:11:14,833 --> 00:11:16,300
You're not using your brains!

271
00:11:16,300 --> 00:11:20,633
[KIDS, WOMAN WAILING]

272
00:11:20,633 --> 00:11:24,967
[OMINOUS MUSIC PLAYING]

273
00:11:24,967 --> 00:11:27,067
- Why?
- What happened?

274
00:11:27,067 --> 00:11:31,000
[CRYING]
They took my Papa, Gabo!

275
00:11:31,000 --> 00:11:32,967
They took Babot, my husband!

276
00:11:32,967 --> 00:11:35,233
And the other guys too!

277
00:11:35,233 --> 00:11:38,133
Those are our family!
Gabo, please help us!

278
00:11:38,133 --> 00:11:39,600
What do the kidnappers
look like?

279
00:11:39,600 --> 00:11:42,300
We didn't see them.
Their faces are covered

280
00:11:42,333 --> 00:11:43,500
and they have guns!

281
00:11:43,500 --> 00:11:47,167
Hold on, the kidnappers
have guns?

282
00:11:47,167 --> 00:11:50,033
Gabo, we should tell
the NLEA about this.

283
00:11:50,033 --> 00:11:51,167
Let's report this now.

284
00:11:51,167 --> 00:11:53,367
There's someone from NLEA
who's always by the block.

285
00:11:53,367 --> 00:11:56,167
- Come on, let's report it!
- Yes, let's go!

286
00:11:56,167 --> 00:11:58,033
- Come on, guys.
- Let's go! Hurry!

287
00:11:58,033 --> 00:11:59,667
Come on, come on!

288
00:11:59,667 --> 00:12:01,100
[GABO] Let's hurry!

289
00:12:01,100 --> 00:12:03,100
[BINOY] There! Take a right!

290
00:12:03,100 --> 00:12:04,133
- [TOLITS] Gabo, tell them!
- [TEKLA] Be careful!

291
00:12:04,133 --> 00:12:06,967
You guys should do it.
Those are my enemies.

292
00:12:06,967 --> 00:12:08,600
Right. They arrested you.

293
00:12:08,600 --> 00:12:11,033
- Tekla, let's do it.
- Okay, let's go.

294
00:12:11,033 --> 00:12:12,667
- [TOLITS] Sir! Sir! Sir!
- [TEKLA] The kids.

295
00:12:12,667 --> 00:12:15,000
Sir, we need help!

296
00:12:15,033 --> 00:12:17,200
Their parents were kidnapped.

297
00:12:17,200 --> 00:12:21,067
[KIDS CRYING]

298
00:12:21,067 --> 00:12:22,367
Gabo.

299
00:12:22,367 --> 00:12:23,900
What do you think happened?

300
00:12:23,900 --> 00:12:25,700
Why did they kidnap
Mister Babot and the others?

301
00:12:25,700 --> 00:12:28,900
Oh, they might kill them.

302
00:12:28,900 --> 00:12:30,233
You think they did them wrong?

303
00:12:30,233 --> 00:12:31,300
I don't think so.

304
00:12:31,300 --> 00:12:32,900
Those guys are nice.

305
00:12:32,900 --> 00:12:34,167
Especially Mister Babot.

306
00:12:34,167 --> 00:12:36,300
Oh, then why would
they kidnap him?

307
00:12:36,300 --> 00:12:38,000
What's the use?

308
00:12:40,200 --> 00:12:41,300
Don't worry.

309
00:12:42,333 --> 00:12:45,200
We'll find out
why they were kidnapped.

310
00:12:45,200 --> 00:12:48,167
[OMINOUS MUSIC CONTINUES]

311
00:12:51,100 --> 00:12:52,233
Who?
Who abducted them?

312
00:12:52,233 --> 00:12:56,167
My husband was taken
by some men. They had guns.

313
00:12:56,167 --> 00:12:59,067
Sir, maybe you can help us.

314
00:12:59,067 --> 00:13:02,733
Ma'am, just head to the station
to file a blotter report.

315
00:13:02,733 --> 00:13:04,900
Oh, there are so
many cases like that.

316
00:13:04,900 --> 00:13:07,067
Mutilated bodies
end up in the river.

317
00:13:07,067 --> 00:13:09,200
That might happen to the parents
of these children.

318
00:13:09,200 --> 00:13:11,667
Hey, watch what you're saying!

319
00:13:11,667 --> 00:13:14,900
Wait, are you serious? We still
need to go to your station?

320
00:13:14,900 --> 00:13:19,500
We can't find their parents now!
What should we do?!

321
00:13:19,500 --> 00:13:22,100
If we go to the station, we
might not find them alive!

322
00:13:22,133 --> 00:13:24,700
Are you even thinking?

323
00:13:24,700 --> 00:13:27,267
Gabo,
looks like they're arguing.

324
00:13:27,267 --> 00:13:28,800
Should we go check on them?

325
00:13:28,800 --> 00:13:30,267
Let's not interfere,

326
00:13:30,267 --> 00:13:33,033
we might get caught
and not find Mister Babot.

327
00:13:34,900 --> 00:13:36,067
There's nothing we can do.

328
00:13:36,067 --> 00:13:38,900
You really need to go to
the station to file a blotter.

329
00:13:38,900 --> 00:13:40,967
Go to the station?
Did you hear yourselves?

330
00:13:40,967 --> 00:13:42,133
What are you even doing there?

331
00:13:42,133 --> 00:13:43,567
- What are you even here for?
- Tekla, Tekla, Tekla.

332
00:13:43,567 --> 00:13:45,300
- Have a heart, please!
- Tekla, let it go.

333
00:13:45,300 --> 00:13:47,700
It looks like we really need
to file a blotter.

334
00:13:47,700 --> 00:13:51,200
- Why do we need to?!
- We have to follow the process.

335
00:13:51,200 --> 00:13:53,233
Fine, fine! Let's go! Let's go!

336
00:13:53,233 --> 00:13:54,633
- Let's go.
- Let's head back there.

337
00:13:54,667 --> 00:13:57,067
[TOLITS] We'll handle this,
okay? We'll take care of it.

338
00:13:57,067 --> 00:13:59,100
- Okay? Don't worry.
- Go home!

339
00:14:01,100 --> 00:14:02,333
So they're just standing around?

340
00:14:02,333 --> 00:14:03,667
That's enough, Tekla.

341
00:14:03,667 --> 00:14:07,833
- Let's go. Let's go.
- [CHILDREN SOBBING LOUDLY]

342
00:14:07,833 --> 00:14:11,833
- Tekla, what did they say?
- Nothing!

343
00:14:11,833 --> 00:14:14,167
That NLEA unit
refuses to help us.

344
00:14:14,167 --> 00:14:19,300
- [BREATHING HEAVILY]
- [OMINOUS MUSIC PLAYING]

345
00:14:19,300 --> 00:14:22,133
We should just take
the kids home.

346
00:14:22,133 --> 00:14:24,800
We'll look for
Mister Babot ourselves.

347
00:14:24,800 --> 00:14:27,967
- That's better. Let's go.
- Come on.

348
00:14:28,000 --> 00:14:29,200
Don't cry anymore.

349
00:14:29,200 --> 00:14:31,033
We'll look for your dad.

350
00:14:31,033 --> 00:14:37,300
[OMINOUS MUSIC CONTINUES]

351
00:14:38,367 --> 00:14:40,700
- [TEKLA] Poor kids.
- [TOLITS] Let's help them.

352
00:14:40,700 --> 00:14:42,700
Someone already
came up to them.

353
00:14:42,700 --> 00:14:45,700
- [SEBASTIAN] Oh, thank you.
- Sam.

354
00:14:45,700 --> 00:14:48,133
Come, stay with them for now.

355
00:14:48,133 --> 00:14:50,633
Come on, sit over there.

356
00:14:50,633 --> 00:14:53,867
- Wow.
- There.

357
00:14:53,867 --> 00:14:57,833
Finish that so you
can feel better, okay?

358
00:14:57,833 --> 00:14:59,700
[SIGHS HEAVILY]

359
00:14:59,700 --> 00:15:02,367
You finally brought him here.

360
00:15:02,400 --> 00:15:03,800
- Hm?
- Hmm.

361
00:15:03,800 --> 00:15:05,900
- Sebastian, right?
- Yes.

362
00:15:05,900 --> 00:15:08,200
Just be patient with my sister,
okay?

363
00:15:08,200 --> 00:15:09,667
She can be very stubborn.

364
00:15:09,667 --> 00:15:12,200
Oh, he's responsible and very
disciplined.

365
00:15:12,200 --> 00:15:15,733
Sam, just say yes to Sebastian!

366
00:15:15,733 --> 00:15:19,233
He's so handsome!
You two look so good together!

367
00:15:19,233 --> 00:15:21,033
[CLEARS THROAT]
You know, Auntie,

368
00:15:21,033 --> 00:15:23,367
I'm letting her take her time.

369
00:15:23,367 --> 00:15:24,567
I'm not rushing her

370
00:15:24,567 --> 00:15:27,900
because I want her
to get to know me better.

371
00:15:27,900 --> 00:15:29,200
Mm-hmm...

372
00:15:29,200 --> 00:15:33,067
Sebastian, I'm just letting you
know that I approve of you.

373
00:15:33,067 --> 00:15:35,700
- Oh, my!
- He just gave me a ride home.

374
00:15:35,733 --> 00:15:37,933
Please don't overthink this.

375
00:15:37,933 --> 00:15:39,200
- Mm-hmm.
- Oh, come on.

376
00:15:39,200 --> 00:15:40,967
Finish that drink, sweetie.

377
00:15:42,267 --> 00:15:45,067
If anything happens to
Samantha Jacinto,

378
00:15:45,067 --> 00:15:49,233
Ricardo will blame no one else
but us.

379
00:15:49,233 --> 00:15:51,733
Just us!

380
00:15:51,733 --> 00:15:54,833
And I'm not afraid of Ricardo.

381
00:15:54,833 --> 00:15:56,400
[SCOFFS]

382
00:15:56,400 --> 00:16:01,033
Let me remind you, even if
he's no longer in service,

383
00:16:01,033 --> 00:16:05,033
he can easily bring us down
if he wants to!

384
00:16:06,867 --> 00:16:08,433
Just let him try.

385
00:16:08,467 --> 00:16:15,367
Let him try, and he'll see the
Mariano who's been holding back

386
00:16:15,367 --> 00:16:19,133
and waiting for the right moment
to get back at him.

387
00:16:19,133 --> 00:16:25,200
[GRIM MUSIC PLAYING]

388
00:16:25,200 --> 00:16:30,267
If you do decide that you'd like
to invest in the project,

389
00:16:30,267 --> 00:16:33,233
please call me, General.

390
00:16:33,233 --> 00:16:35,800
Sure, I will, so I can beat
the other investors to it.

391
00:16:35,800 --> 00:16:38,133
- Thank you for dropping by.
- You're most welcome.

392
00:16:38,133 --> 00:16:40,933
- Go ahead, Manny.
- I'll walk you out, General.

393
00:16:40,933 --> 00:16:42,000
All right.

394
00:16:44,500 --> 00:16:45,733
Dad?

395
00:16:48,500 --> 00:16:51,767
Dad?
Um... I just...

396
00:16:51,767 --> 00:16:54,400
I just wanted to tell you
something.

397
00:16:54,400 --> 00:16:56,900
It's about... work.

398
00:16:58,467 --> 00:17:01,333
You gave up the Zafra case?

399
00:17:01,333 --> 00:17:05,133
And I want this case closed.

400
00:17:06,900 --> 00:17:10,000
I just lost my temper with the
criminal we caught.

401
00:17:10,000 --> 00:17:12,700
He disrespected me.
I hit him, and...

402
00:17:14,433 --> 00:17:16,300
I was suspended.

403
00:17:19,433 --> 00:17:21,100
You got suspended?!

404
00:17:23,500 --> 00:17:25,467
- What's happening?
- Dad, I'm sorry.

405
00:17:25,467 --> 00:17:28,133
I warned you to drop that case.

406
00:17:29,200 --> 00:17:31,033
But you remained headstrong.

407
00:17:31,033 --> 00:17:33,767
You've brought such shame
to my name, Sam.

408
00:17:35,367 --> 00:17:38,867
But the reality...
The truth of the matter is...

409
00:17:38,867 --> 00:17:41,500
my daughter is stubborn.

410
00:17:41,500 --> 00:17:45,367
And now,
you're suspended from work.

411
00:17:45,367 --> 00:17:47,100
And you can even lose your job!

412
00:17:49,400 --> 00:17:51,133
I can already hear
people saying,

413
00:17:51,133 --> 00:17:54,533
"Look, that's General Jacinto's
daughter!

414
00:17:54,533 --> 00:17:58,100
His useless kid
who's an NCIA agent!"

415
00:17:59,900 --> 00:18:03,233
[CLEARS THROAT]
Sir, excuse me.

416
00:18:03,233 --> 00:18:08,500
She's not useless.
She's the best agent at NCIA.

417
00:18:08,500 --> 00:18:11,133
Her? The best?

418
00:18:11,133 --> 00:18:13,500
No wonder the NLEA
is leaving you in the dust.

419
00:18:13,500 --> 00:18:16,800
Sir, I understand
that you're upset.

420
00:18:16,800 --> 00:18:19,400
Sam only did what she had to do

421
00:18:19,400 --> 00:18:21,467
to get answers
from the criminal.

422
00:18:21,500 --> 00:18:24,533
And she did all of this in line
with her duty.

423
00:18:27,167 --> 00:18:31,400
I can't believe this, Sam.
You even brought a defender!

424
00:18:31,400 --> 00:18:33,067
Only one thing is clear.

425
00:18:34,233 --> 00:18:37,067
You tarnished the Jacinto name!

426
00:18:39,833 --> 00:18:41,233
You are a disgrace!

427
00:18:42,933 --> 00:18:44,167
Ricardo...

428
00:18:45,600 --> 00:18:47,500
- Dad!
- Sam.

429
00:18:47,500 --> 00:18:50,833
Sorry. I'm sorry, everyone,
that you had to witness this.

430
00:18:50,833 --> 00:18:52,600
I'm sorry.
I'm so sorry.

431
00:18:52,600 --> 00:18:56,500
Give them some time.
Come on. Let me walk you out.

432
00:18:58,867 --> 00:19:01,467
Dad.
Dad, I'm sorry.

433
00:19:01,467 --> 00:19:03,267
I am asking for your
forgiveness.

434
00:19:03,267 --> 00:19:07,033
Everything I do
is for the service.

435
00:19:07,033 --> 00:19:09,433
I do everything to prove to you

436
00:19:09,433 --> 00:19:11,300
that I deserve to be
your daughter too.

437
00:19:11,300 --> 00:19:18,233
[EMOTIONAL MUSIC PLAYING]

438
00:19:18,233 --> 00:19:19,933
You're asking for forgiveness?

439
00:19:21,267 --> 00:19:23,067
Do you think that erases
what you did?

440
00:19:23,067 --> 00:19:24,467
That your suspension
will be lifted?

441
00:19:24,467 --> 00:19:27,400
That the stain on my name
will be wiped clean?!

442
00:19:27,400 --> 00:19:29,200
Dad, I'm sorry.

443
00:19:29,233 --> 00:19:34,333
All my mistakes, all my faults,
they won't affect your legacy.

444
00:19:34,333 --> 00:19:38,500
I promise you that.
I am the only one to blame.

445
00:19:38,500 --> 00:19:43,333
[EMOTIONAL MUSIC CONTINUES]

446
00:19:43,333 --> 00:19:45,167
That's easy for you to say.

447
00:19:45,167 --> 00:19:48,467
Every move you make,
people are watching me.

448
00:19:49,600 --> 00:19:55,033
Every mistake you make
is my embarrassment!

449
00:19:58,133 --> 00:19:59,867
- Dad--
- You listen to me, Sam!

450
00:20:02,200 --> 00:20:05,500
It's not just shame
you brought to our family.

451
00:20:08,600 --> 00:20:11,333
You also brought us
so much pain.

452
00:20:16,100 --> 00:20:20,400
RJ is gone because
of what you did.

453
00:20:21,367 --> 00:20:25,567
I had so many dreams for him,
for our family.

454
00:20:27,133 --> 00:20:28,667
Now, everything is gone.

455
00:20:33,033 --> 00:20:34,167
[INHALES SHARPLY]

456
00:20:34,167 --> 00:20:35,900
Do you know what's left?

457
00:20:37,233 --> 00:20:38,533
Do you?!

458
00:20:38,533 --> 00:20:43,133
[EMOTIONAL MUSIC CONTINUES]

459
00:20:43,133 --> 00:20:45,300
The scar of what you did!

460
00:20:47,500 --> 00:20:51,533
[SNIFFLES]
I'm sorry. I'm sorry.

461
00:20:52,567 --> 00:20:57,033
Dad, all of us here are hurting
over RJ being gone,

462
00:20:57,033 --> 00:20:59,067
especially me.

463
00:20:59,067 --> 00:21:02,000
Every day I am consumed
by guilt.

464
00:21:02,000 --> 00:21:03,133
[SNIFFLES]

465
00:21:03,133 --> 00:21:04,700
And every day I pray

466
00:21:04,700 --> 00:21:07,667
that you'll find it in you
to forgive me too.

467
00:21:07,667 --> 00:21:11,267
[BREATHING HEAVILY, SOBBING]

468
00:21:12,600 --> 00:21:14,700
I don't think that's ever
going to happen.

469
00:21:14,700 --> 00:21:21,567
[HEARTBREAKING MUSIC PLAYING]

470
00:21:25,667 --> 00:21:27,333
As a matter of fact,

471
00:21:30,433 --> 00:21:32,200
sometimes I wish...

472
00:21:36,567 --> 00:21:39,133
it was you
who was gone instead.

473
00:21:43,733 --> 00:21:45,633
Ricardo!

474
00:21:45,633 --> 00:21:52,533
[HEARTBREAKING MUSIC CONTINUES]

475
00:21:53,600 --> 00:22:00,000
[SNIFFLES, SOBS]

476
00:22:17,833 --> 00:22:18,667
Ricardo!

477
00:22:18,667 --> 00:22:20,833
You can't defend
your daughter now.

478
00:22:20,833 --> 00:22:23,567
Remember, I warned her
many times about this case.

479
00:22:23,567 --> 00:22:28,100
Don't you feel bad for her?
She was suspended!

480
00:22:28,967 --> 00:22:32,000
How could you say
those hurtful things to her?!

481
00:22:32,000 --> 00:22:33,933
Isobel, I'm a general.

482
00:22:33,933 --> 00:22:36,300
The girls grew up
knowing that fact.

483
00:22:38,133 --> 00:22:40,233
I'm not like other fathers.

484
00:22:40,233 --> 00:22:43,833
I won't hesitate to shame them
if they're being a disgrace.

485
00:22:43,833 --> 00:22:45,133
Why are you acting like this?

486
00:22:46,233 --> 00:22:49,033
Do you know who
she is going up against?

487
00:22:51,200 --> 00:22:52,367
Do you?!

488
00:22:52,367 --> 00:22:54,833
[MOROSE MUSIC PLAYING]

489
00:22:54,833 --> 00:22:58,133
You should've just helped her
solve this case.

490
00:22:58,867 --> 00:23:01,333
But no,
you kept going against her!

491
00:23:01,333 --> 00:23:03,333
Can you stop meddling, Isobel?

492
00:23:05,967 --> 00:23:08,300
I kept trying to keep her
off the case...

493
00:23:10,133 --> 00:23:13,100
because it's what's best
for her career.

494
00:23:16,200 --> 00:23:19,100
But she disobeyed me.
Now, look what happened.

495
00:23:20,867 --> 00:23:22,333
She was suspended.

496
00:23:22,367 --> 00:23:27,733
[MOROSE MUSIC CONTINUES]

497
00:23:27,733 --> 00:23:29,200
I'm just...

498
00:23:30,367 --> 00:23:33,400
I'm just glad she didn't cause
another death in this family.

499
00:23:33,400 --> 00:23:40,200
[MOROSE MUSIC CONTINUES]

500
00:23:51,067 --> 00:23:53,400
[DARK MUSIC PLAYING]

501
00:23:53,400 --> 00:23:56,367
Keep tabs on Samantha Jacinto's
every move.

502
00:23:59,000 --> 00:24:01,767
We have to get rid of her
as soon as possible.

503
00:24:01,767 --> 00:24:04,867
Copy, boss.
We'll take care of it.

504
00:24:04,867 --> 00:24:07,233
Are you sure about your plan?

505
00:24:07,233 --> 00:24:09,267
Ma'am Deborah is right.

506
00:24:09,267 --> 00:24:12,933
If we lay a finger
on Samantha Jacinto,

507
00:24:12,933 --> 00:24:14,400
I'm sure...

508
00:24:16,667 --> 00:24:19,200
...her father will get back
at us.

509
00:24:19,200 --> 00:24:23,267
What do you want us
to do then, Lee? Spare her?

510
00:24:23,267 --> 00:24:25,933
She's the agent
who arrested Victor

511
00:24:25,933 --> 00:24:27,867
and shot Lucas.

512
00:24:27,867 --> 00:24:30,000
All I'm saying is...

513
00:24:30,033 --> 00:24:32,433
if we're going to eliminate her,

514
00:24:32,433 --> 00:24:36,000
we must be prepared
for the consequences.

515
00:24:36,867 --> 00:24:37,933
Lee.

516
00:24:38,800 --> 00:24:40,233
I'm prepared.

517
00:24:41,267 --> 00:24:44,033
And I'm not scared
of General Jacinto.

518
00:24:46,267 --> 00:24:48,467
If he tries to get back at us,

519
00:24:48,467 --> 00:24:51,433
I'll send him to his grave
right next to his daughter.

520
00:24:51,433 --> 00:24:55,733
[DARK MUSIC CONTINUES]

521
00:24:55,733 --> 00:24:57,100
Move!

522
00:25:00,200 --> 00:25:02,767
This will be your
last day on earth, Samantha.

523
00:25:04,000 --> 00:25:07,967
[GUNSHOTS]

524
00:25:07,967 --> 00:25:10,733
- [GUNSHOTS]
- [SCREAMING]

525
00:25:10,733 --> 00:25:17,433
[DARK MUSIC SWELLS]

526
00:25:19,733 --> 00:25:26,500
[CRYING]

527
00:25:26,500 --> 00:25:33,467
[MELANCHOLIC MUSIC PLAYING]

528
00:25:40,300 --> 00:25:44,000
Please help us get Babot
and the others back.

529
00:25:44,000 --> 00:25:47,033
Those evil men might kill them!

530
00:25:47,033 --> 00:25:51,267
Mister Gabo!
Please bring back my father!

531
00:25:51,267 --> 00:25:58,200
[CRYING CONTINUES]

532
00:25:58,200 --> 00:25:59,200
Stop crying now.

533
00:25:59,200 --> 00:26:01,500
We've reported what happened
to the police.

534
00:26:01,500 --> 00:26:03,367
If they won't take action,

535
00:26:03,367 --> 00:26:05,433
we'll find your fathers
ourselves.

536
00:26:06,200 --> 00:26:08,333
Did you hear that?

537
00:26:08,333 --> 00:26:10,333
Don't cry anymore.

538
00:26:10,367 --> 00:26:12,500
Your fathers
will come home, okay?

539
00:26:12,500 --> 00:26:13,833
Hush now.

540
00:26:13,833 --> 00:26:15,300
Gabo.

541
00:26:15,500 --> 00:26:18,300
Who do you think could've taken
Mister Babot and the others?

542
00:26:18,300 --> 00:26:21,800
And why would they
take innocent people?

543
00:26:21,800 --> 00:26:24,467
Yeah, and they won't get
anything from Babot.

544
00:26:24,467 --> 00:26:26,967
They have no money
to pay for ransom.

545
00:26:26,967 --> 00:26:28,867
[CRYING CONTINUES]

546
00:26:28,867 --> 00:26:32,467
Could they have been
abducted for their organs?

547
00:26:32,467 --> 00:26:34,933
You know, for human trafficking.

548
00:26:35,400 --> 00:26:40,833
Every year, we hear of cases
like that happening in our area.

549
00:26:40,833 --> 00:26:44,367
You probably didn't know because
you were in jail, but it's true.

550
00:26:45,500 --> 00:26:47,167
[DABOY] Yes, that's true.

551
00:26:47,167 --> 00:26:49,467
It's mostly kidneys
those guys are after.

552
00:26:51,167 --> 00:26:52,533
[TOLITS] Gabo.

553
00:26:52,933 --> 00:26:56,033
It's likely they abducted
Mister Babot and the others...

554
00:26:57,533 --> 00:27:01,500
...to harvest their organs
and sell them to foreigners.

555
00:27:03,267 --> 00:27:04,600
Gabo!

556
00:27:04,600 --> 00:27:07,567
[CRYING CONTINUES]

557
00:27:07,567 --> 00:27:11,367
That means this
will happen again.

558
00:27:12,433 --> 00:27:15,133
I'm sure those kidnappers
will come back here.

559
00:27:17,100 --> 00:27:18,333
Ma'am...

560
00:27:18,933 --> 00:27:23,233
We promise you that we
will find Mister Babot.

561
00:27:25,400 --> 00:27:28,233
Thank you so much, Gabo,
for helping us.

562
00:27:28,233 --> 00:27:35,167
[CRYING CONTINUES]

563
00:27:38,567 --> 00:27:39,867
Let's go!

564
00:27:39,867 --> 00:27:43,300
[CRYING CONTINUES]

565
00:27:43,300 --> 00:27:44,533
Stop crying now.

566
00:27:47,567 --> 00:27:51,467
We really can't rely on
anyone but ourselves.

567
00:27:51,500 --> 00:27:54,833
I hope we find Mister Babot
and the others alive.

568
00:27:54,833 --> 00:27:56,233
I'm afraid we're too late.

569
00:27:56,233 --> 00:28:00,000
If our hunch is right that they
were abducted for their organs,

570
00:28:00,000 --> 00:28:02,000
we might not find them alive.

571
00:28:02,000 --> 00:28:05,000
The question is,
where do we even start?

572
00:28:05,000 --> 00:28:07,633
We can start by asking around.

573
00:28:07,633 --> 00:28:09,867
I'm sure someone saw
what happened.

574
00:28:11,567 --> 00:28:12,567
Gabo.

575
00:28:15,300 --> 00:28:17,400
I know where they were taken.

576
00:28:19,900 --> 00:28:22,000
I didn't come forward earlier
because the NLEA was here.

577
00:28:22,000 --> 00:28:23,533
They could be accomplices.

578
00:28:24,600 --> 00:28:29,433
[STIRRING MUSIC PLAYING]

579
00:28:29,433 --> 00:28:30,533
Where?

580
00:28:30,533 --> 00:28:33,333
Follow me. I'll take you there.
Let's use my jeep.

581
00:28:37,633 --> 00:28:40,567
Are you sure we can trust Edwin?

582
00:28:41,467 --> 00:28:44,767
We have no other option
but to trust him

583
00:28:44,767 --> 00:28:46,933
if we want to find
Mister Babot and the others.

584
00:28:48,433 --> 00:28:49,400
Let's go.

585
00:28:50,033 --> 00:28:51,033
Come on.

586
00:28:51,033 --> 00:28:58,000
[STIRRING MUSIC CONTINUES]

587
00:29:05,700 --> 00:29:07,133
[ENGINE SPUTTERS ON]

588
00:29:07,133 --> 00:29:08,900
[ENGINE REVVING]

589
00:29:08,900 --> 00:29:11,800
Gabo, are you sure about this?

590
00:29:11,800 --> 00:29:13,967
Those men are heavily armed.

591
00:29:13,967 --> 00:29:16,967
This is suicide. We don't have
a single weapon on us!

592
00:29:16,967 --> 00:29:18,600
Why should we be afraid?

593
00:29:19,467 --> 00:29:20,767
We are from Tondo.

594
00:29:21,633 --> 00:29:23,500
We fight with our hearts.

595
00:29:23,500 --> 00:29:25,100
We have nothing to fear.

596
00:29:26,667 --> 00:29:27,967
Gabo is right.

597
00:29:27,967 --> 00:29:31,967
We grew up fighting to survive.
We won't bow down to them.

598
00:29:33,400 --> 00:29:36,000
If we're going to die
trying to save Mister Babot

599
00:29:36,000 --> 00:29:38,533
and our other neighbors,
then so be it.

600
00:29:38,533 --> 00:29:41,833
What matters is we did
something good with our lives.

601
00:29:41,833 --> 00:29:48,467
[STIRRING MUSIC CONTINUES]

602
00:29:51,200 --> 00:29:53,633
<i> If we don't act now, when?</i>

603
00:29:54,367 --> 00:29:57,233
<i>There has been a spike
in abduction cases in Manila.</i>

604
00:29:57,900 --> 00:30:00,667
<i> Gabo, are you sure about this?</i>

605
00:30:01,933 --> 00:30:05,700
<i>Those men are heavily armed.
This is suicide.</i>

606
00:30:06,600 --> 00:30:08,867
<i> We have to act now.</i>

607
00:30:08,867 --> 00:30:11,800
<i> We can't just let this go on.</i>

608
00:30:11,800 --> 00:30:14,467
<i> Betchay is the new manager
of BeerGin Bar.</i>

609
00:30:14,467 --> 00:30:16,567
<i> Your father is doing me dirty.</i>

610
00:30:16,567 --> 00:30:18,867
<i>Just say the word,
and I'll handle it.</i>

611
00:30:18,867 --> 00:30:20,867
<i> I already shot Gabo's father.</i>

612
00:30:20,867 --> 00:30:22,533
<i>I can easily do the same
to his stepmother.</i>

613
00:30:22,533 --> 00:30:24,833
<i> Is it true? You shot him?</i>

614
00:30:25,700 --> 00:30:28,633
<i>Listen up.
Our target is Mr. Chan.</i>

615
00:30:28,633 --> 00:30:30,767
<i>Take down anyone
who gets in our way.</i>

616
00:30:31,633 --> 00:30:35,767
<i>The Zafras are ruthless.
They don't fight fair.</i>

617
00:30:35,800 --> 00:30:38,400
<i>The moment I find out
your parents are involved,</i>

618
00:30:38,400 --> 00:30:40,000
<i>you can all enjoy
jail time together.</i>

619
00:30:40,000 --> 00:30:42,667
<i>They think they're
above the law.</i>

620
00:30:42,667 --> 00:30:43,900
- [SCREAMS]
- [WHIMPERS]

621
00:30:43,900 --> 00:30:46,300
<i>Well, Samantha?!
You still alive?!</i>

622
00:30:46,300 --> 00:30:47,600
<i> Don't let her get away!</i>

623
00:30:48,333 --> 00:30:50,333
<i>Release Samantha
and this will all be over.</i>

624
00:30:50,333 --> 00:30:52,667
<i>You know you're standing
in my territory, Ricardo.</i>

625
00:30:52,667 --> 00:30:55,833
<i>Don't you want to
make it out of here alive?</i>

626
00:30:55,833 --> 00:30:57,633
<i> I need a job.</i>

627
00:30:58,600 --> 00:30:59,900
<i> I need money.</i>

628
00:30:59,900 --> 00:31:01,467
Get back here!

629
00:31:01,467 --> 00:31:02,967
<i> Where did Gabo get the money?</i>

630
00:31:02,967 --> 00:31:04,400
<i> Pops, I hope you can help me.</i>

631
00:31:04,400 --> 00:31:05,767
<i>- We know nothing!
- We know nothing!</i>

632
00:31:05,767 --> 00:31:07,667
<i> - Nothing? Really?
- Really. Nothing at all.</i>

633
00:31:07,667 --> 00:31:08,967
<i> Don't mess with me!</i>

634
00:31:09,000 --> 00:31:11,267
Even if you threaten to kill us,
<i> we have nothing to say!</i>

635
00:31:11,267 --> 00:31:12,500
<i> Fine. Kill them.</i>

636
00:31:12,500 --> 00:31:14,000
<i> I really need a job.</i>

637
00:31:14,000 --> 00:31:15,833
<i> I can give you a mission,</i>

638
00:31:15,833 --> 00:31:17,833
<i>but I don't know
if you're ready.</i>

639
00:31:17,833 --> 00:31:19,833
<i> There's a reason we met.</i>

640
00:31:19,833 --> 00:31:22,833
<i> And that's to bring justice
for our loved ones</i>

641
00:31:22,833 --> 00:31:24,867
<i> and help those in need.</i>

642
00:31:24,867 --> 00:31:26,533
<i> I accept the mission.</i>

643
00:31:26,533 --> 00:31:30,300
<i>Give Gabo all the weapons
he will need.</i>
